    "id": 6,
    "options": {
      "content": "**Depth is not throughput.** Active and dead-lettered panels show average point-in-time queue depth. Flat zero can mean no traffic or messages consumed between samples. A flat nonzero DLQ can be retained messages; it is not a count of new failures. Use incoming/outgoing totals alongside depth.\n\n**Missing is not zero.** Gaps, No data, or query errors can mean absent telemetry, ingestion delay, wrong time range, or missing access. Check the last 6 hours, expand to 24 hours if needed, and inspect errors. Nulls are not connected or filled with zeros.\n\n**Container Apps:** system-event counts come from existing workspace logs. They do not prove readiness or uptime. Raw messages, synthetic traffic, new diagnostics and alert rules are not included. Managed-identity log-query access requires a Grafana runtime smoke check.\n\n**Cost:** 5-minute refresh; existing resources only. Grafana may scale to zero, so the first load can be slow. Log queries may incur existing workspace query charges depending on the table plan.\n\n**Overview analytics:** traffic cards/bars sum observed Azure Total buckets separately for each queue over the selected range. These are partial subtotals if telemetry is missing, not lifetime totals or unique incidents across pipeline stages. Count > 0 filtering suppresses empty/all-null totals; observed zero stays zero. Depth cards use the last reported interval Average, which may be stale; inspect time-series timestamps and gaps.\n\n**Circular indicator:** the donut compares only observed incoming traffic by queue. Zero traffic has no meaningful share; missing telemetry means incomplete coverage. No capacity, utilization, or failure percentage is inferred. Gauges are omitted because no verified limit/threshold exists.\n\n**Query cost:** added summary panels reuse the same metric definitions but issue additional read-only metric queries; refresh remains five minutes. No new log query or resource is introduced.",
      "mode": "markdown"
    },
    "title": "How to Read This Dashboard",
    "type": "text"
  },
